{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-ex-13","title":"rem:pet-ch2-ex-13","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":871,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#rem:pet-ch2-ex-13","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-killing-field]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-19]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"rem:pet-ch2-ex-13","line":1751,"source":"\\begin{remark}[Affine vector fields]\n  \\label{rem:pet-ch2-ex-13}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0090}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection, def:pet-ch2-killing-field, def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor, rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation, prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries, rem:pet-ch3-ex-19, def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean, rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean, ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:2.5.13}\n  A vector field is \\emph{affine} when\n  $L_X\\nabla=0$. Every Killing field is affine. The converse fails on\n  $\\mathbb{R}^n$: the radial field $X(x)=x$ is affine but not Killing. Both\n  statements are formalized.\n  \\sketch\n  For Killing $X$, $\\nabla X$ is skew-adjoint. Differentiation, the Ricci\n  identity \\cref{rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation}, and the curvature\n  symmetries of \\cref{prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries} give Kostant's formula\n  $\\nabla^2_{U,V}X=-R(X,U)V$. Together with\n  \\[\n    (L_X\\nabla)(U,V)=R(X,U)V+\\nabla^2_{U,V}X\n  \\]\n  from \\cref{rem:pet-ch3-ex-19}, this gives $L_X\\nabla=0$. For $X(x)=x$,\n  $\\nabla_VX=V$ and $\\nabla^2X=0$; Euclidean flatness makes it affine, while\n  $(L_Xg)(v,v)=2|v|^2$.\n\\end{remark}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Remark</div></section>[Affine vector fields] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368322d65782d3133\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0090</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection\">↗ def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-killing-field\">↗ def:pet-ch2-killing-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-curvature-tensor\">↗ def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23rem%3Apet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation\">↗ rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-curvature-symmetries\">↗ prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23rem%3Apet-ch3-ex-19\">↗ rem:pet-ch3-ex-19</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean\">↗ def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23rem%3Apet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean\">↗ rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23ex%3Apet-ch3-euclidean-flat\">↗ ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.5.13</span></span>A vector field is <em>affine</em> when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_X\\nabla =0$\">$L_X\\nabla =0$</span>. Every Killing field is affine. The converse fails on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb {R}^n$\">$\\mathbb {R}^n$</span>: the radial field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X(x)=x$\">$X(x)=x$</span> is affine but not Killing. Both statements are formalized. \\sketch For Killing <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla X$\">$\\nabla X$</span> is skew-adjoint. Differentiation, the Ricci identity <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23rem%3Apet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368332d72696363692d6964656e746974792d64657269766174696f6e\">subsection rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation</a>, and the curvature symmetries of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-curvature-symmetries\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368332d6375727661747572652d73796d6d657472696573\">subsection prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries</a> give Kostant&#x27;s formula <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla ^2_{U,V}X=-R(X,U)V$\">$\\nabla ^2_{U,V}X=-R(X,U)V$</span>. Together with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  (L_X\\nabla )(U,V)=R(X,U)V+\\nabla ^2_{U,V}X  \\]\">\\[  (L_X\\nabla )(U,V)=R(X,U)V+\\nabla ^2_{U,V}X  \\]</span> from <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23rem%3Apet-ch3-ex-19\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-19\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368332d65782d3139\">section rem:pet-ch3-ex-19</a>, this gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_X\\nabla =0$\">$L_X\\nabla =0$</span>. For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X(x)=x$\">$X(x)=x$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _VX=V$\">$\\nabla _VX=V$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla ^2X=0$\">$\\nabla ^2X=0$</span>; Euclidean flatness makes it affine, while <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(L_Xg)(v,v)=2|v|^2$\">$(L_Xg)(v,v)=2|v|^2$</span>. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-ex-12","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-ex-14","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection","title":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection","label":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-killing-field","title":"def:pet-ch2-killing-field","label":"def:pet-ch2-killing-field"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor","label":"def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation","label":"rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries","title":"prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries","label":"prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-19","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-19","label":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-19"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean","label":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean","title":"rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean","label":"rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat","title":"ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat","label":"ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-ex-13","title":"rem:pet-ch2-ex-13","tex":"\\begin{remark}[Affine vector fields]\n  \\label{rem:pet-ch2-ex-13}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0090}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection, def:pet-ch2-killing-field, def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor, rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation, prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries, rem:pet-ch3-ex-19, def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean, rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean, ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:2.5.13}\n  A vector field is \\emph{affine} when\n  $L_X\\nabla=0$. Every Killing field is affine. The converse fails on\n  $\\mathbb{R}^n$: the radial field $X(x)=x$ is affine but not Killing. Both\n  statements are formalized.\n  \\sketch\n  For Killing $X$, $\\nabla X$ is skew-adjoint. Differentiation, the Ricci\n  identity \\cref{rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation}, and the curvature\n  symmetries of \\cref{prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries} give Kostant's formula\n  $\\nabla^2_{U,V}X=-R(X,U)V$. Together with\n  \\[\n    (L_X\\nabla)(U,V)=R(X,U)V+\\nabla^2_{U,V}X\n  \\]\n  from \\cref{rem:pet-ch3-ex-19}, this gives $L_X\\nabla=0$. For $X(x)=x$,\n  $\\nabla_VX=V$ and $\\nabla^2X=0$; Euclidean flatness makes it affine, while\n  $(L_Xg)(v,v)=2|v|^2$.\n\\end{remark}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection","title":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-connection","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-killing-field","title":"def:pet-ch2-killing-field","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ricci-identity-derivation","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries","title":"prop:pet-ch3-curvature-symmetries","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-19","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-19","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-euclidean","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean","title":"rem:pet-ch2-killing-field-euclidean","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat","title":"ex:pet-ch3-euclidean-flat","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}